  heading="Thermal Imaging"
  lead="Active thermography: infrared imaging used to locate air leakage and thermal defects in the building envelope."
  photo="Thermal image of a wall or ceiling"
>
  <h2>What thermography shows</h2>
  <p>An infrared camera displays surface temperature differences. In buildings, those patterns can reveal air leakage, missing or compressed insulation, and thermal bridging that aren't visible to the eye.</p>
  <p>Active thermography creates controlled conditions, such as a pressure difference across the envelope, so these defects show up clearly in the images.</p>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Builders and design teams checking envelope details, and homeowners who want to see where heat and air are escaping.</p>

